---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Tailor-made Tours — Seoul Walking Tours">
  <div class="bg-natural-light">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="bg-medium-chromatic-teal pt-section-lg pb-section">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-22 lg:px-32">
        <div class="reveal">
          <!-- <p class="accent-label text-light-atmospheric-teal-70 mb-4">
            TAILOR-MADE TOURS
          </p> -->
          <h1
            class="text-section font-semibold text-natural-light leading-tight mb-4"
          >
            Tailor-made Tours
          </h1>
          <p class="text-xl italic text-light-atmospheric-teal-70">
            Seoul, made to measure.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Body text -->
    <section class="py-section">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-22 lg:px-32">
        <div
          class="max-w-3xl space-y-6 leading-relaxed text-natural-dark-210 reveal"
        >
          <p>
            Seoul is generous with its highlights — the palaces, the markets,
            the parks, the neighbourhoods each with a character entirely their
            own. Most visitors arrive with a list of things to do and places to
            visit, and the list is a good one. But somewhere underneath it,
            lingers a question that is harder to answer: what else is there?
            What does this city look like if I turn away from where everyone
            else is looking?
          </p>
          <p>
            That's where I come in. With extensive knowledge of the city and its
            different areas, I can help you find what you're looking for — even
            before you know exactly what it is. Tell me when you're here, how
            long you have, and what interests you. I'll take it from there and
            come back with a few ideas.
          </p>
          <p>
            Seoul is a city still catching its breath — five hundred years of
            dynasty, a brutal colonial period, a war that split the peninsula,
            and then a sprint from poverty to prosperity the world is still
            trying to understand. Markets that feed half the city, mountains
            that rise straight from the city centre, neighbourhoods shaped by
            poets, factory workers, and artists. A morning at a Buddhist temple
            tucked away behind a lively street. An evening among local youth in
            a park along the Han river. A hole-in-the-wall lunch in a place no
            guidebook has found yet.
          </p>
          <p>
            Beyond the better-known landmarks, the themes I know well include
            Korean contemporary history, everyday neighbourhood life, Korean
            film and literature, market and food culture. But the tour doesn't
            have to start with a theme — tell me when you're here and how long
            you have, and I'll put something together. If something falls
            outside what I know well, I'll say so.
          </p>
          <p>
            My tours are walking conversations. No flag, no microphone. We
            explore together, at a pace that allows for detours. Pricing depends
            on duration and group size — get in touch and we'll work out the
            details.
          </p>
          <p class="italic text-black/50">
            Tell me when you're arriving and what you're hoping for. A few lines
            are enough.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Duration row -->
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="bg-medium-chromatic-teal py-section-lg">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-22 lg:px-32">
        <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-8 items-center reveal">
          <div class="flex-1">
            <h2 class="text-subsection font-semibold text-natural-light mb-3">
              Get in touch
            </h2>
            <p class="text-light-atmospheric-teal-70 leading-relaxed">
              A few lines about when you're arriving and what interests you is
              all I need.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="shrink-0">
            <a
              href="mailto:contact@jitsejager.com"
              class="inline-block bg-accent-orange-23 px-10 py-4 rounded-full text-natural-light font-semibold hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity whitespace-nowrap"
            >
              contact@jitsejager.com
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
